{{unc|pt}}. Different origins are proposed, including:
* {{uder|pt|tpw|paranãbuku}} ("long river") or ''para’nã'' ("river") + ''buka'' ("hole").
* {{m|pt|Pernão Boca}} or {{m|pt|Pernambuka}}, approximations of how natives referred to "Boca de Fernão", an old name for the Santa Cruz channel.

